### Tunisian License Validation API Tests
### Use this with REST Client extension in VS Code or import to Postman

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000
@contentType = application/json

### Test 1: Validate License (Base64) - Without Signup
POST {{baseUrl}}/professionals/validate-license
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "licenseImage": "data:image/jpeg;base64,/9j/4AAQSkZJRg..."
}

###
# Expected Response (Success):
# {
#   "isValid": true,
#   "licenseNumber": "12345678",
#   "reason": "License validated successfully",
#   "extractedText": "REPUBLIQUE TUNISIENNE...",
#   "confidence": "high",
#   "tunisianKeywordsFound": ["tunisie", "permis de conduire"]
# }
###

### Test 2: Professional Signup with License Validation
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/signup/professional
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "professional@example.com",
  "password": "SecurePassword123!",
  "fullName": "Ahmed Ben Ali",
  "licenseImage": "data:image/jpeg;base64,/9j/4AAQSkZJRg...",
  "locations": [
    {
      "name": "Main Branch",
      "address": "Avenue Habib Bourguiba, Tunis",
      "lat": 36.8065,
      "lon": 10.1815
    }
  ]
}

###
# Expected Response (Success):
# {
#   "message": "Professional account registered successfully",
#   "licenseNumber": "12345678",
#   "confidence": "high",
#   "professionalId": "64f1a2b3c4d5e6f7g8h9i0j1"
# }
###

### Test 3: Login as Professional
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "professional@example.com",
  "password": "SecurePassword123!"
}

###
# Expected Response:
# {
#   "access_token": "eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIs...",
#   "refresh_token": "eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIs...",
#   "role": "professional",
#   "email": "professional@example.com",
#   "id": "64f1a2b3c4d5e6f7g8h9i0j1",
#   "username": "Ahmed Ben Ali"
# }
###

### Test 4: Get All Professionals
GET {{baseUrl}}/professionals
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

###

### Test 5: Get Professional by ID
@professionalId = 64f1a2b3c4d5e6f7g8h9i0j1
GET {{baseUrl}}/professionals/{{professionalId}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

###

### Test 6: Invalid License - Non-Tunisian Document
POST {{baseUrl}}/professionals/validate-license
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "licenseImage": "data:image/jpeg;base64,iVBORw0KGgoAAAANSUhEUgAAAAEAAAABCAYAAAAfFcSJAAAADUlEQVR42mNk+M9QDwADhgGAWjR9awAAAABJRU5ErkJggg=="
}

###
# Expected Response (Failure):
# {
#   "statusCode": 400,
#   "message": "License validation failed",
#   "reason": "This does not appear to be a Tunisian driver's license..."
# }
###

### Test 7: Duplicate License - Try to register same license twice
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/signup/professional
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "another@example.com",
  "password": "SecurePassword123!",
  "fullName": "Fatma Ben Hassan",
  "licenseImage": "data:image/jpeg;base64,/9j/4AAQSkZJRg..."
}

###
# Expected Response (Failure):
# {
#   "statusCode": 400,
#   "message": "License validation failed",
#   "reason": "This license number is already registered in our system."
# }
###

### Notes:
### 1. Replace base64 strings with actual Tunisian license images
### 2. Convert images to base64 using: https://www.base64-image.de/
### 3. Or use CLI: base64 -i license.jpg | pbcopy
### 4. Ensure backend is running: npm run start:dev
### 5. Check logs for detailed validation information


